  Proprietary and confidential.

  Registers StuckArchiveStateReconciler as an actual Nuxeo component (not
  just an extension contribution): it needs its own start() lifecycle hook
  to run once the repository is guaranteed to be up, so it must be a full
  component with an <implementation>, ordered after
  ComponentStartOrders.REPOSITORY (see the class's own
  getApplicationStartedOrder() override for the exact value).

  It reconciles any broadcast:archiveState left stuck in a transient
  archive-pending / restore-pending state by an unclean shutdown, matching
  the metadata back to the actual physical blob location in MinIO. A
  healthy system has no stuck documents, so on a normal boot this is a
  no-op.
-->
<component name="com.mam.platform.core.archiveReconciler" version="1.0">

  <implementation class="com.mam.platform.core.archive.StuckArchiveStateReconciler" />

</component>
